{% chart type="bar" eyebrow="Head office location, start of 2026" title="UK private sector businesses by English region and nation" data="London:1006830|South East:864215|East of England:563360|North West:550825|South West:531405|West Midlands:435905|Yorkshire and the Humber:430875|East Midlands:356310|North East:162890|Scotland:359210|Wales:195995|Northern Ireland:128995" highlight="London" source="Business population estimates 2026, detailed Table 9, published 5 November 2026" /%}

A business with sites in more than one region is counted only where it is registered. These counts therefore differ from where people work. Regional estimates are less precise than the UK total. The release gives coefficients of variation from 2% for the South East to 6% for the North East.

## Why do the ONS and the government give different counts?

They count different things on different dates. The government estimate covers the private sector at the start of the year and includes an estimate of unregistered businesses. The ONS count covers businesses registered for VAT and/or PAYE.

| | Business population estimates 2026 | ONS, UK business: activity, size and location 2026 |
|---|---|---|
| Figure | 5,586,835 | 2,786,985 |
| Who is counted | Private sector businesses, registered and unregistered | Businesses registered for VAT and/or PAYE, across legal statuses |
| Includes government and non-profit bodies | No | Yes: 3,205 central government, 9,260 local authority and 84,505 non-profit rows |
| Date | Start of 2026 | Snapshot taken on 13 March 2026 |
| Unregistered businesses | Estimated from the ONS Labour Force Survey and HMRC self-assessment data (2.9 million) | Not included |
| Published | 5 November 2026 | 24 September 2026 |

Sources: [Business population estimates 2026](https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/business-population-estimates-2026/business-population-estimates-for-the-uk-and-regions-2026-statistical-release) and [ONS bulletin, Table 1 and data sources](https://www.ons.gov.uk/businessindustryandtrade/business/activitysizeandlocation/bulletins/ukbusinessactivitysizeandlocation/2026).

The 2026 release says its 2.7 million registered private sector businesses (48% of the total) are recorded by ONS. I have not tried to reconcile 2.7 million with 2,786,985. The ONS figure includes public sector and non-profit bodies and uses a different snapshot date.

The two sources also moved in opposite directions this year. The ONS reports 2,786,985 businesses, an increase of 1.9% from March 2025. The government estimate fell because of unregistered businesses, which the ONS count does not include.

One more definition matters. The release says the register behind its registered counts "only includes those companies registered for VAT and/or PAYE, rather than all those recorded on the Companies House register". A count of limited companies from Companies House is a different number again.

## What the figures include and leave out

- **Private sector only.** The release excludes the government and not-for-profit sectors. It includes public corporations and nationalised bodies.
- **Registered and unregistered.** Registered businesses come from the ONS Inter-Departmental Business Register. Unregistered businesses are estimated from the ONS Labour Force Survey and HMRC self-assessment tax return data.
- **Net change only.** The release "cannot be used to estimate numbers of business start-ups or closures". It points to ONS Business Demography for births and deaths.
- **One employee counts as none.** A company with a single employee director is treated as having no employees.
- **No unregistered companies.** The release assumes no unregistered company is an active business and says that assumption will be reviewed.
- **Turnover excludes SIC 2007 Section K.** Financial and insurance turnover is left out because it is not available on a comparable basis.
- **Head office basis.** Counts and their employment and turnover sit in the region of the head office.
- **Status.** It is official statistics in development, not accredited official statistics. The release gives 5,587,000 with a 95% interval of plus or minus 109,000 and a coefficient of variation of 1%.
- **Next edition.** The release says the next publication is scheduled for autumn 2027.

## Sources and methodology

| Source | Publisher | Published | Reference date | Used for |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| [Business population estimates for the UK and regions 2026: statistical release](https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/business-population-estimates-2026/business-population-estimates-for-the-uk-and-regions-2026-statistical-release) | Department for Business, Innovation, Science and Trade | 5 November 2026 | Start of 2026 | All 2026 counts, shares and notes |
| [BPE 2026 detailed tables (xlsx)](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ae3162ec591dbfc31fb67f0/BPE_2026_detailed_tables.xlsx) | Department for Business, Innovation, Science and Trade | 5 November 2026 | Start of 2026 | Tables 1, 3, 9 and 25 |
| [Business population estimates for the UK and regions 2025: statistical release](https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/business-population-estimates-2025/business-population-estimates-for-the-uk-and-regions-2025-statistical-release) | Department for Business and Trade | 2 October 2025 | Start of 2025 | 2025 comparison figures |
| [UK business; activity, size and location: 2026](https://www.ons.gov.uk/businessindustryandtrade/business/activitysizeandlocation/bulletins/ukbusinessactivitysizeandlocation/2026) | Office for National Statistics | 24 September 2026 | 13 March 2026 | The VAT and/or PAYE register count |

Limits that apply to every figure on this page:

- These are estimates with sampling error, mostly from the unregistered group. A change of 1.8% in the total is smaller than the uncertainty around it.
- The 2026 and 2025 editions use different departmental names. The 2026 release names the Department for Business, Innovation, Science and Trade and the 2025 release names the Department for Business and Trade. I use the name each release gives.
- Where a figure is "not stated" in the table above, the release text does not give a change and I have not calculated one, apart from the one subtraction I label as mine.
- I have not used estimates from third-party pages. Every figure comes from the releases linked above.

For businesses that buy search work, the question is rarely the national count. It is how many competitors sit in your own size band, industry and region. My [guide to what SEO costs](/services/how-much-does-seo-cost/) covers the price side, and the [SEO ROI calculator](/tools/seo-roi-calculator/) lets you test it with your own numbers.

## How to cite this page

Cite the release for any figure you publish. Safe wording follows this pattern:

> There were 5,586,835 private sector businesses in the UK at the start of 2026, of which 4,115,175 (74%) had no employees (Business population estimates 2026, Department for Business, Innovation, Science and Trade, published 5 November 2026).

To cite this comparison page: Sunny Patel, "How many businesses are there in the UK? 2026 figures", sunnypatel.co.uk/blog/uk-business-statistics/, last checked 24 November 2026.
